b70/ — Intel Arc Pro B70 additions to this exllamav3 fork

This directory builds on the work of others. Their copyright notices and
license terms are reproduced below.

1. ExLlamaV3 and the EXL3 format
   https://github.com/turboderp-org/exllamav3
   Copyright (c) 2025 Turboderp
   License: MIT (see ../LICENSE in this repository)

   The quantizer in b70/quantize/ writes EXL3-format tensors and follows the
   EXL3 per-channel scaling order of exllamav3 v1.4.2
   (exllamav3/modules/quant/exl3_lib/quantize.py). The models used for the
   checks are turboderp's Qwen3.8-27B EXL3 quantizations
   (https://huggingface.co/turboderp/Qwen3.8-27B-exl3).

2. exl3xpu — EXL3 inference on Intel Arc as a vLLM XPU plugin
   https://github.com/sybil-solutions/exl3xpu (formerly github.com/0xSero/exl3xpu)
   Container image ghcr.io/0xsero/exl3xpu (version 0.1.0)
   Copyright (c) 2026 0xSero
   License: MIT

   b70/serve/patches/*.patch modify exl3xpu 0.1.0 files
   (csrc/exl3_ops.sycl, exl3xpu/vllm_plugin.py). b70/serve/tests/check_mixedk.py
   imports exl3xpu's ref.py and plugin classes inside that image. The
   quantizer's tests and export self-checks use exl3xpu's ref.py as the
   decode reference (not redistributed here).

